SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Trumpeter ***\nAnge
 ls - Trumpeter — Costume (you provide): Fitted black shorts\, white fi
 tted shirt\; Shoes: White ballet shoes\; Makeup: Men's Light Stage Makeu
 p\; Hair: Neat\, out of the eyes/face\; Prop (BA provides): Trumpet\nLig
 ht Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Li
 ght brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•
  Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush
  on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed 
 out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Make
 up:\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner - apply from corner to corner\n• Br
 own or tan under cheek bone to create shadow and accentuate the jaw line
 \n• Brown eye liner around lips and nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *
 Men will not look like they are wearing makeup. It will help the face be
  seen from the stage.\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and f
 lesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pi
 eces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•
  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the p
 oint of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never throw costumes 
 or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n
 • Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n• Do not attem
 pt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• Ne
 ver apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to re
 frain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n• Refrain f
 rom the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• Never wear
  any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handle or consume f
 ood or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n• Do n
 ot remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theate
 r\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs followi
 ng their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comp
 ly fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policie
 s\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that ma
 y damage or stain costumes.
