 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nTime: 9:00 PM–9:30 PM.\nIn Performance Co
 stumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — production week.\n\n*** STANDIN
 G RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dancers should be check-in and ba
 ckstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Time.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals 
 (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiving and Production Week Rehea
 rsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named.\n
 SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and 
 the BA portal are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/s
 preadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTU
 ME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Trumpeter ***\nAngels - Trumpeter — Costume (yo
 u provide): Fitted black shorts\, white fitted shirt\; Shoes: White ball
 et shoes\; Makeup: Men's Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Neat\, out of the ey
 es/face\; Prop (BA provides): Trumpet\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sh
 eet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow applied t
 o the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and
  black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to app
 ly plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• 
 Red or Dark Red lipstick\nMen's Stage Makeup:\n• Dark Brown/Black eyel
 iner - apply from corner to corner\n• Brown or tan under cheek bone to
  create shadow and accentuate the jaw line\n• Brown eye liner around l
 ips and nude/flesh colored lipstick\n• *Men will not look like they ar
 e wearing makeup. It will help the face be seen from the stage.\nDancers
  of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostu
 me Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing 
 to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkans
 as in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter 
 how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, 
 or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on th
 e floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, o
 r launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while 
 in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on
  costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume o
 r cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to c
 ast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costu
 me\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their 
 assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins u
 sed to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all h
 eadpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all upda
 tes to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, p
 aints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
